From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: linux-a9 <linux-a9@localhost>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:45:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 19/21] media: apple: vxd: copy only the printed fence fields in the
 mbox dump

The debugfs mbox dump copied all sixteen struct apple_vxd_fence under
the lock to print five fields of each.  Every fence carries a struct
completion, which lockdep makes large: with the QEMU smoke's KASAN +
PROVE_LOCKING config the frame reached 2176 bytes, over the 2048-byte
limit (-Wframe-larger-than).  Copy just the state, id, type, error and
status.

Signed-off-by: linux-a9 <linux-a9@localhost>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <maintainer@example.invalid>
---
 drivers/media/platform/apple/vxd/apple-vxd-mbox.c | 21 +++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/vxd/apple-vxd-mbox.c b/drivers/media/platform/apple/vxd/apple-vxd-mbox.c
index 466d8c069a362d39b19ea0176ff215283df8cd3e..b030d70d48886b2d01aaa7f232b8eb9d577e41ca 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/vxd/apple-vxd-mbox.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/vxd/apple-vxd-mbox.c
@@ -1180,7 +1180,18 @@ static int apple_vxd_mbox_dump_show(struct seq_file *m, void *v)
 	struct apple_vxd_dev *vxd = m->private;
 	struct apple_vxd_mbox_stats st;
 	struct apple_vxd_ring to_mtx, to_host;
-	struct apple_vxd_fence fences[APPLE_VXD_NUM_FENCES];
+	/*
+	 * Only what the dump prints: a whole struct apple_vxd_fence carries a
+	 * struct completion, which lockdep makes large (a 16-entry copy
+	 * overflowed the 2 KiB frame limit in the QEMU smoke's KASAN build).
+	 */
+	struct {
+		enum apple_vxd_fence_state state;
+		u16 id;
+		u8 type;
+		bool error;
+		u32 status;
+	} fences[APPLE_VXD_NUM_FENCES];
 	u32 raw_mtx, raw_host, rd, wr;
 	unsigned long flags;
 	bool ready;
@@ -1196,7 +1207,13 @@ static int apple_vxd_mbox_dump_show(struct seq_file *m, void *v)
 	to_mtx = vxd->to_mtx;
 	to_host = vxd->to_host;
 	st = vxd->stats;
-	memcpy(fences, vxd->fences, sizeof(fences));
+	for (i = 0; i < APPLE_VXD_NUM_FENCES; i++) {
+		fences[i].state = vxd->fences[i].state;
+		fences[i].id = vxd->fences[i].id;
+		fences[i].type = vxd->fences[i].type;
+		fences[i].error = vxd->fences[i].error;
+		fences[i].status = vxd->fences[i].status;
+	}
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&vxd->mbox_lock, flags);
 
 	raw_mtx = vxd_read(vxd, VXD_REG_TO_MTX_RING);
